{
 "format": 1,
 "version": "1.2.0",
 "min_shell": 1,
 "notes": [
  "Folders with emoji: make your own, and move, pin or archive notes (hold one, or drag). Tags with #, and better search.",
  "Paste a link and it becomes a tidy chip. Headings, lists that carry on when you press Enter, a Read view, Undo, word count, files and voice memos in notes.",
  "Draw and write by hand with the S Pen (pressure-sensitive; your palm is ignored), and mark up pictures.",
  "Type a date like \"test fri 9am\" and Vault asks if you want a reminder. Plus an Upcoming week, flash cards, a focus timer and repeating checklists.",
  "See pictures before you send them, and use Vault on a Chromebook (or any browser).",
  "A Files tab: browse the PC folders you choose from your phone, and keep files in Vault Drive.",
  "Safety nets: note history with Restore, \"Download everything\", weekly PC backups, and a conflict copy instead of lost words."
 ],
